\section{Discussion}

\subsection{Integrated interpretation across the two trials}
\begin{itemize}
  \item \lead{SQDG falling is the most informative result, because it contradicts
        the canonical phosphate-starvation response}, in which phospholipids are
        replaced by non-phosphorus glycolipids and SQDG should \emph{rise}. So
        this is not simple phosphate starvation, but some mix of nutrient
        limitation, temperature, developmental state and plastid-membrane
        turnover that this design cannot separate.
  \item TG accumulation comes with reorganised DG--TG coordination rather than a
        uniform rise in neutral lipids -- ratios involving TG, DG, PE and MGDG all
        shift toward TG, the PS--TG correlation changes sign, and the LINEX
        balances split by branch direction.
  \item PS and lysophospholipid shifts are directionally robust but confined to
        pools under 0.2\% of TIC, so they represent redistribution within small
        pools rather than bulk membrane change.
  \item Genetic architecture is strongly environment-dependent, and
        genotype-by-nutrient effects cannot be separated from genotype-by-year or
        genotype-by-management effects.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{A TIFY/JAZ cluster recovered in both trials}
\begin{itemize}
  \item Four TIFY paralogues in a 290~kb stretch on chromosome~1, \lead{recovered
        under both regimes but reporting different lipids} -- nine 16:0-containing
        storage triacylglycerols under CTL, versus an ether lipid, an
        18:3-containing phosphatidylcholine and a free C20:3 fatty acid under LIN.
  \item Mechanistically tight rather than coincidental, since jasmonate is
        synthesised from $\alpha$-linolenic acid released from plastid
        galactolipids and JAZ proteins are the repressors of jasmonate signalling.
  \item Cold support in three systems -- rice (cold-induced, ABA-independent),
        pepper (silencing confers cold sensitivity, overexpression improves
        tolerance) and sweet orange.
  \item Unlike the other tandem loci, this enrichment rests on two independent
        250~kb intervals rather than one.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Under CTL, membrane organization and amino-acid metabolism}
\begin{itemize}
  \item A phospholipid-transporting ATPase provides the clearest membrane-lipid
        link.
  \item The tyrosine locus is the more interesting half. Tyrosine degradation runs
        through tyrosine aminotransferase and 4-hydroxyphenylpyruvate dioxygenase
        to homogentisate and then to fumarate and \lead{acetoacetate, which feeds
        acetyl-CoA} -- the substrate for fatty-acid synthesis. Every phenotype at
        that locus is a triacylglycerol.
  \item The same amino acid is committed to dhurrin under LIN, so tyrosine is a
        branch point the two trials resolve differently.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Under LIN, nitrogen candidates}
\begin{itemize}
  \item Three nitrate transporters from two families -- an NRT2.1-like
        high-affinity transporter, an NPF/NRT1 transporter carrying the strongest
        LIN single-lipid association, and an OsNPF2.4 orthologue.
  \item Nitrogen also appears in a \emph{storage} rather than uptake role. A
        chromosome~1 locus overlapping the dhurrin cluster links seven candidates
        to fatty-acid and PA-ratio traits, and four of the seven carry annotations
        covering the pathway in turn -- a CYP71E1-reaction monooxygenase
        ($r^2=1.00$), a glycosyltransferase, a MATE-family transporter and a
        glutathione transferase.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Under LIN, phosphorus and sulfur converge on SQDG}
\begin{itemize}
  \item An SPX-domain phosphate-status signalling protein, a SULTR3-family plastid
        sulfate transporter, and a PHT1-family phosphate transporter.
  \item \lead{The argument.} SQDG is a sulfolipid whose head group is built from
        sulfur imported into the plastid. Phosphate limitation alone should
        \emph{increase} SQDG through phospholipid replacement, yet SQDG was
        depleted -- which makes restricted plastidic sulfate supply a plausible
        alternative hypothesis.
  \item The PHT1 transporter associates with neutral storage lipids rather than
        phospholipids, again the opposite of what simple
        phospholipid-to-glycolipid replacement predicts.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Under LIN, a cold-induced MADS regulator}
\begin{itemize}
  \item \texttt{SORBI\_3003G406800}, a MADS-box transcription factor and the
        \lead{strongest LIN fatty-acid association in the panel}
        ($p=2.7\times10^{-17}$), with the lead SNP inside the gene ($r^2=1$) and
        the signal recurring across 13 phenotypes.
  \item Cold-induced in sorghum within six hours and a hub of the early
        shock-phase co-expression module.
  \item Its closest annotated maize homologue at 84\% identity is
        \textit{ZmMADS69}, the flowering-time QTL acting upstream of ZmRap2.7 to
        relieve repression of the florigen \textit{ZCN8}.
  \item LIN was planted early specifically to impose cold, and cold acclimation
        proceeds partly through acyl-chain remodelling, which makes fatty-acid
        traits the expected point of contact. The association may reflect direct
        regulation of lipid metabolism or a shift in developmental stage at
        sampling; this design cannot separate them.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Reaction-supported remodeling candidates under LIN}
\begin{itemize}
  \item A non-specific phospholipase~C6 feeding the DG node from the phospholipid
        pool -- \lead{but linkage cannot separate it from five sterol C-8
        isomerase genes in the same 137~kb window}, which opens an alternative
        chemistry for branch~(i) through sterol esterification rather than a
        PDAT-like transfer.
  \item \textit{DGAT1} is the clearest genetic link to the TG phenotype, sitting
        under a repeatedly mapped chromosome~10 QTL for crude fat, with five of
        six associated phenotypes polyunsaturated triacylglycerols.
  \item An \textit{SDP1}-like patatin lipase covers the reverse arm, associating
        with total TG and the TG/SQDG ratios rather than with individual species.
  \item A sphingolipid module -- three genes spanning three consecutive pathway
        steps on three chromosomes, all associated with the same ether lipid.
\end{itemize}

